<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">Chapter 31</p>
    <h2 id="t-arrow">Where the Arrow Comes From</h2>
    <p class="lede">&ldquo;Here is the most dangerous question anyone has asked this framework, and it
      deserves a plain answer.&rdquo;</p>
    <p>If the structure is encoded as the fixed roots of one equation &mdash; roots that never move, never
      rearrange, never interact &mdash; then there is exactly one way the system can be. One configuration.
      And the number of possible configurations is what determines entropy: the quantity whose increase
      drives the arrow of time, the reason ice melts and cups break and we remember the past but not the
      future. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p>
    <p><strong>One configuration means zero entropy. Zero entropy means no arrow.</strong> The essay exists
      to say that out loud rather than hide it in a footnote: &ldquo;It is the framework's hardest problem,
      and naming it is more honest than solving it with&rdquo; &mdash; and the sentence that follows refuses
      the easy repair.</p>
    <p class="muted">The reply the framework does offer &mdash; that the counting inherits its asymmetry
      from the geometry, the denser infinity below one supplying a slope &mdash; is taken up at
      <a href="/stress-tests/#t-entropy">the entropy objection</a>, where it is also conceded to be the
      weakest joint in the structure.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <h2 id="t-ledger">Earned, chosen, refused</h2>
    <dl class="glossary">
      <dt>Earned</dt>
      <dd><span class="formula-inline">\(P_n=F_{n+2}-1\)</span> and
        <span class="formula-inline">\(\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}n^{-2}=\pi^2/6\)</span> are theorems. Hawking radiation
        and the time-dependence of the 68 : 27 : 5 split are established physics. The Bullet Cluster
        constraint and the \(10^{-122}\) discrepancy are real targets, not straw ones.</dd>
      <dt>Chosen</dt>
      <dd>Reading the horizon as a leaking seam; reading the cell cycle as a completed octave; taking
        333/666/999 as a scaled image of &minus;1, 0 and 1; and the conjecture that where the returners pile
        is where the numbers crowd. Each is a way of seeing that the evidence permits and does not compel.</dd>
      <dt>Refused</dt>
      <dd>The claim that any of this predicts an experiment. The claim that a derivation of a moving target
        is a derivation. The claim that zero entropy can be waved away. And the flattery of a machine that
        never says <em>hang on</em>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

