<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">&mdash; a note on where the essays discharge</p>
    <h2 id="t-essays-feed">What the Essays Are Load-Bearing For</h2>
    <p>These eleven are placed last and read as a coda, which undersells them. Four of the chapters above
      are doing structural work elsewhere in the volume, and it is worth saying which, so that a reader who
      skips this part knows what they have skipped.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#t-number">Chapter 23, <em>A Number Made of Itself</em></a>, is the licence for the whole
        of Part I. Without the distinction between a measured constant and a precondition, the claim that π
        is not found inside the universe is a flourish. With it, it is the premise the chain of necessity
        hangs from &mdash; which is why it is restated at
        <a href="/foundations/#t-pi-made">the foundations</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="#t-cell">Chapter 26, <em>The Cell Keeps the Beat</em></a>, supplies the substrate for the
        integral self. An integral needs a dx, and the circadian oscillator is the evidence that biology
        provides one without being asked. See <a href="/the-self/#t-beat">the beat below the self</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="#t-three-numbers">Chapter 29, <em>Three Numbers Everything Hangs From</em></a>, is the
        skeleton: 0, 1 and &minus;1 as the fixed points of scaling, multiplication and inversion. Every
        later structure &mdash; the densities, the poles at 0 and 999, the vertices at 333 and 666 &mdash;
        is that skeleton rescaled.</li>
      <li><a href="#t-arrow">Chapter 31, <em>Where the Arrow Comes From</em></a>, is the framework's
        weakest joint and its most important one, and it is the reason the entropy objection in
        <a href="/stress-tests/#t-entropy">the stress tests</a> is conceded rather than answered.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">The three retractions remain the best writing here. A volume that can say <em>this
      part does not work</em> in its own voice has earned more trust than one that cannot, and the
      framework is deliberately at its most convincing where it is admitting what it cannot do.</p>
  </div>
</section>
